  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"45\" data-end=\"289\"><strong data-start=\"45\" data-end=\"93\">Free Beta hCG (human chorionic gonadotropin)</strong> refers to the <strong data-start=\"108\" data-end=\"129\">unbound &beta;-subunit</strong> of hCG, a hormone produced by the placenta during pregnancy. It is also used as a <strong data-start=\"212\" data-end=\"228\">tumor marker</strong> and in <strong data-start=\"236\" data-end=\"258\">prenatal screening</strong> for chromosomal abnormalities.</p>\n<p data-start=\"296\" data-end=\"317\"><strong data-start=\"300\" data-end=\"317\">Clinical Uses</strong></p>\n<ol data-start=\"318\" data-end=\"660\">\n<li data-start=\"318\" data-end=\"361\">\n<p data-start=\"321\" data-end=\"361\"><strong data-start=\"321\" data-end=\"359\">Pregnancy detection and monitoring</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"362\" data-end=\"485\">\n<p data-start=\"365\" data-end=\"410\"><strong data-start=\"365\" data-end=\"387\">Prenatal screening</strong> (first trimester) for:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"414\" data-end=\"485\">\n<li data-start=\"414\" data-end=\"446\">\n<p data-start=\"416\" data-end=\"446\"><strong data-start=\"416\" data-end=\"446\">Down syndrome (Trisomy 21)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"450\" data-end=\"485\">\n<p data-start=\"452\" data-end=\"485\"><strong data-start=\"452\" data-end=\"485\">Edwards syndrome (Trisomy 18)</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"486\" data-end=\"660\">\n<p data-start=\"489\" data-end=\"510\"><strong data-start=\"489\" data-end=\"505\">Tumor marker</strong> for:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"514\" data-end=\"660\">\n<li data-start=\"514\" data-end=\"597\">\n<p data-start=\"516\" data-end=\"597\"><strong data-start=\"516\" data-end=\"554\">Gestational trophoblastic diseases</strong> (e.g., hydatidiform mole, choriocarcinoma)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"601\" data-end=\"660\">\n<p data-start=\"603\" data-end=\"660\"><strong data-start=\"603\" data-end=\"623\">Germ cell tumors</strong> (e.g., testicular or ovarian cancer)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p data-start=\"1184\" data-end=\"1226\"><strong data-start=\"1188\" data-end=\"1226\">Interpretation by Clinical Context</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"1228\" data-end=\"1259\"><strong data-start=\"1233\" data-end=\"1259\">1. Pregnancy Detection</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1260\" data-end=\"1491\">\n<li data-start=\"1260\" data-end=\"1333\">\n<p data-start=\"1262\" data-end=\"1333\"><strong data-start=\"1262\" data-end=\"1274\">Positive</strong>: Free &beta;-hCG detectable within <strong data-start=\"1305\" data-end=\"1332\">7&ndash;10 days of conception</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1334\" data-end=\"1417\">\n<p data-start=\"1336\" data-end=\"1417\">Levels rise rapidly in early pregnancy, doubling approximately every 48&ndash;72 hours.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1418\" data-end=\"1491\">\n<p data-start=\"1420\" data-end=\"1491\">Slower rise may suggest <strong data-start=\"1444\" data-end=\"1465\">ectopic pregnancy</strong> or <strong data-start=\"1469\" data-end=\"1490\">early miscarriage</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1493\" data-end=\"1553\"><strong data-start=\"1498\" data-end=\"1553\">2. Prenatal Screening (1st Trimester Combined Test)</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"1554\" data-end=\"1563\">Includes:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1564\" data-end=\"1660\">\n<li data-start=\"1564\" data-end=\"1576\">\n<p data-start=\"1566\" data-end=\"1576\">Free &beta;-hCG</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1577\" data-end=\"1625\">\n<p data-start=\"1579\" data-end=\"1625\">PAPP-A (Pregnancy-Associated Plasma Protein A)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1626\" data-end=\"1660\">\n<p data-start=\"1628\" data-end=\"1660\">Nuchal translucency (ultrasound)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
